NO BUNDLED SECURITY ENGINES

AppSec Framework bundles no external security engine and downloads none at
runtime. It can invoke ZAP, Nuclei and a source analyser (opengrep or Semgrep);
those are separate programs that the operator installs, running as separate
processes under their own licences. Hadrian is named in `appsec doctor` as a tool
that would cover authorization testing, and is reported there as not integrated:
no code in this project invokes it.

Semgrep's registry rules are licensed under the Semgrep Rules License v1.0, which
permits use only for the user's own internal business purposes and forbids
distribution or provision as a service. AppSec Framework therefore never ships,
vendors, bundles or auto-fetches Semgrep registry rules, and its documentation
and defaults do not reference registry rule packs.
